  "abstract_summary": "Frozen vision-language models often match concepts mentioned in a caption without respecting their negation: a query \"a kitchen with no toaster\" favors an image containing a toaster. Yet these models are substantially stronger at matching affirmative descriptions. We exploit this asymmetry with Negation-Aware Eviden...",
